--- WEB SOURCE PARITY (the spec) ---
DrivingCoachSection({ coachData: DrivingCoachData | undefined }) is a PRESENTATIONAL child of the Driving-Dynamics
page; its only hook is useTranslation. The parent owns the query (useDrivingCoach -> /analytics/driving-coach) and
passes coachData down. Composition (each panel ALWAYS renders, with its own friendly empty sub-state — never a
hidden surface):
  * Section heading "Driving Coach".
  * 3-up row: RadialGauge(overall_score, max 100, green/amber/red arc by band) + "{count} drives analyzed" caption;
      Style Breakdown (stacked bar of efficient/moderate/aggressive over total_drives_analyzed + legend with counts,
      or EmptyState "Drive more to see your style breakdown."); two StatCards (Avg / Best Efficiency, Wh/km).
  * Weekly Score Trend LineChart when weekly_trend.length > 1, else EmptyState "Need at least 2 weeks...".
  * Driving Patterns: 5 label/percentage/threshold bars (Hard Acceleration lo20/hi40, Hard Braking 15/30, Highway
      50/70, Short Trips (<5 km) 30/50, Cold Starts 15/30); value<=lo green, <=hi amber, else red.
  * Recommendations: impact Badge (high=danger/medium=warning/low=success) + tip, or EmptyState "Recommendations
      will appear after more drives.".
  * Per-Drive Scores DataTable (Date | Score badge | Style badge | Wh/km | Distance) or EmptyState "Drive data will
      appear after your first trip.". Score badge >=75 success / >=50 warning / else danger; Style efficient=success
      / moderate=warning / aggressive=danger. fmtNumber default = 2 decimals; formatDateShort = "MMM d".

--- NATIVE REPRODUCTION ---
2-file presentational surface mirroring the established BatteryHealthSection split (P1/S8 state-holder seam — the
parent owns the query and supplies the lifecycle state; the view never performs HTTP and raises RetryRequested):
  * DrivingCoachSection.Model.cs : DrivingCoachSectionState (Loading/Ready/Empty/Error/Stale/Offline);
      DrivingCoachData (+ CoachStyleBreakdown / CoachPatterns / CoachWeeklyPoint / CoachRecommendationItem /
      CoachDriveScore) — pure data, the web coachData prop; DrivingCoachSectionModel (Status + Data + freshness)
      with Loading/Empty/Failed/Ready/Stale/Offline factories; the full Display projection (score gauge band, style
      segments + legend, efficiency stats, weekly-trend gate, pattern thresholds, recommendation impact, per-drive
      rows) via DrivingCoachSectionProjection.Project; DrivingCoachSectionRegistration (slug); PII-safe
      DrivingCoachSectionDiagnostics. No WinUI types — unit-tested headless.
  * DrivingCoachSection.cs        : WinUI 3 view (ContentControl). Renders every state — Loading skeleton chrome
      (polite LiveRegion), Empty (heading + EmptyState), Error (TsQueryError + Retry -> RetryRequested), and the
      Ready/Stale/Offline composition: TsRadialGauge + caption, the style stacked bar (proportional star-grid) +
      legend, two TsStatCard, TsLineChart weekly trend, five threshold pattern bars, recommendation cards
      (TsBadge + tip), and the per-drive badge table (Date + Score TsBadge + Style TsBadge + Wh/km + Distance in a
      scrollable star-grid). Stale/offline freshness chip in the header. Built from shared components only
      (@/components/ui/charts/data-display/feedback/motion equivalents); TsFadeIn honours reduce-motion.
  * gauge band: TsRadialGauge tints its arc from a themed ChartRole (no arbitrary hex like the web RadialGauge), the
      established OptimizerSection precedent; the web green/amber/red SCORE BAND is carried verbatim by the per-drive
      Score / Style badges (same >=75 / >=50 thresholds) and is unit-tested via DrivingCoachSectionProjection.ScoreBand.
  * i18n: the web dynamics.coach.* keys are pre-seeded by P1/S10 in Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw
      (incl. drivesAnalyzed "{0} drives analyzed"). The three style labels the web reads via
      t('dynamics.coach.style.${key}') were the only missing keys; added dynamics.coach.style.{efficient,moderate,
      aggressive} to all three locale catalogs (English placeholders, matching the rest of the pre-seeded coach
      namespace; he/ar are placeholder-translated like the existing entries). Generic column headers map to existing
      catalog keys (translation.Date/Score/Style/Distance, units.whkm). No English literal is hardcoded in native code.
  * a11y: surface AutomationProperties.Name per state; gauge / stat-cards / legend rows / pattern rows / recommendation
      cards / per-drive rows each carry a Narrator name; decorative glyphs + bars are AccessibilityView=Raw; loading
      announced via a polite LiveRegion; reduce-motion honoured by TsFadeIn / TsSkeleton; Group automation peer.
  * Telemetry: view.opened slug=DrivingCoachSection emitted once on Loaded (P1/S11), PII-safe (never logs a score,
      efficiency, distance, style or drive id).

